592186045443] [17592186302305 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "24196412-03d6-5e5f-92de-8b242613ba34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302305 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $C$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -3 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,0\\,\\, & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-1$ and ${u}_{33}=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}=(-1)\\cdot 7=-7.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186321455 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321455 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321455 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "270358e1-4881-5ad1-a4f8-851bd75c0c95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321803 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "536f50c1-40ed-5335-a15d-d507caadcd44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321973 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321973 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321973 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "692d45b1-b07d-5219-a5a6-fb5c7f417996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322011 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322011 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322011 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f6a2bf